==English==

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb|head=[[cross]] the [[line]]}}

# To cross the [[equator]], as a [[vessel]] at [[sea]].
# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} To [[overstep]] a [[boundary]], [[rule]], or [[limit]]; to go too far or do something unacceptable.
#: ''I can tolerate a lot, but they really '''crossed the line''' when they broke the window.''
# {{context|cinematography|lang=en}} to film from the opposite side of an imaginary axis on set in order to view the actors from the opposite direction.

